# Caddy config for theblueai.org. Caddy 2.
#
# theblueai.org is the FRONT DOOR. The whiteboard and the MCP server are things
# running behind it, not the site itself. Until 2026-08-04 the apex just 301'd
# to a Bluesky profile and the front pages lived on the whiteboard subdomain,
# which had the information architecture exactly one level too deep.

# --- the front door -----------------------------------------------------
# Serves the sign-in / create-account pages, the explainers, and "who we are".
# Same backend as the whiteboard: it's one app, routed by path.
theblueai.org, www.theblueai.org {
	encode gzip
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8092
}

# --- the whiteboard -----------------------------------------------------
# Same backend. The app notices it's on the whiteboard.* hostname and sends
# "/" straight to the board rather than the front page.
whiteboard.theblueai.org {
	encode gzip
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8092
}

# NOTE — pds.theblueai.org and bsky-mcp.theblueai.org keep whatever blocks they
# already have. Don't route them through :8092.

# WHY NOT file_server
# -------------------
# An earlier version of the whiteboard block served the frontend off disk and
# proxied only /api/*, /healthz and /ws/*:
#
#     handle {
#         root * /srv/whiteboard
#         try_files {path} /index.html
#         file_server
#     }
#
# That works, and it puts a copy of the built frontend on the host that nothing
# in the deploy pipeline updates. The backend image already contains the
# frontend (backend/Dockerfile stage 1 builds it into /app/static), so after a
# successful `git pull && docker compose up -d --build` the container had the
# new SPA while Caddy kept serving a copy written weeks earlier. /healthz
# returned 200 and the API behaved correctly throughout. It went unnoticed for
# weeks.
#
# The backend handles every path the split config handled by hand:
#   /api/*     -> routes.router (mounted at /api)
#   /ws/*      -> ws_routes.router
#   /oauth/*   -> oauth_routes.router
#   /healthz   -> main.healthz
#   /assets/*  -> StaticFiles mount (immutable, 1yr)
#   /img/*     -> real files from the frontend's public/ dir
#   everything else -> serve_spa returns index.html (the SPA fallback)
#
# Caddy 2 proxies WebSocket upgrades natively, so /ws/* needs no special
# matcher. `encode gzip` is worth keeping: the bundle is ~1.3 MB uncompressed,
# ~420 KB gzipped.

# APPLYING THIS
# -------------
#   cp /pds/caddy/etc/caddy/Caddyfile /pds/caddy/etc/caddy/Caddyfile.bak-$(date +%F)
#   # replace the old theblueai.org redirect block and the whiteboard block
#   docker exec caddy caddy validate --config /etc/caddy/Caddyfile
#   docker exec caddy caddy reload  --config /etc/caddy/Caddyfile
#
# Validate before reloading: that one file also fronts the PDS and bsky-mcp, so
# a syntax error takes all three down rather than just this.
#
# DNS: theblueai.org and www both need A records pointing at the VPS, grey
# cloud (DNS only) so Caddy can complete the ACME challenge itself.
